  "notes": "Gain trim from the guided single-magnet run of 2026-08-24 (captures/magcal_20260824_153205.npz): head driven along its own axis past a fixed magnet, four poses a quarter turn apart, so every sensor was measured at the same closest approach and NO geometry weighting was needed -- the 1/r^3 spread cancels by construction rather than being modelled. Raw peaks spanned only 1.29x across the 16, so this is a small residual gain correction on top of the SPI harmonisation to gain 3000, which is what it should be. It does NOT set absolute scale or fix chip orientation; the Earth-field roll sweep is what does that."
